# Immortals making and unmaking: load, clone, purge, advance, restore and peace, then reboot. In the temple (3001),
# with Hassan: Smokegod (60), Seraph (56) and Decimus (10). load puts what can be taken in the inventory and the rest
# on the floor. clone copies a bag with what's in it, and a mob with what it carries: Hassan's clone shows his
# scimitar wielded, though it was never equipped (#71). At trust 55 Seraph can clone a long sword and the fido but
# not the scimitar or Hassan. Pickpocket (13) envenoms a dagger, and its clone has the poison and the extra
# description Smokegod strings onto it; a clone of the donation pit goes on the floor. Decimus, made hungry and given
# more hit points than he has, eats a poisoned bread; restore cures and heals him, and his room, and every player
# (passing over a connection still at the greeting). advance raises Decimus with three random draws a level, then
# lowers him to level 1 and raises him again. peace calms the aggressive fido. purge empties the room of mobs and
# objects, and disintegrates a player (who's saved first) but not one of the same trust or above. Last, reboot echoes
# and closes every connection.
@obj 3011 3001 18 12 0 1 0
@connect god
Smokegod
smoke123
@return
@return
@connect ser
Seraph
smoke123
@return
@return
@connect dec
Decimus
psswrd
@return
@return
@connect pick
Pickpocket
psswrd
@return
